    "body": "## Problem\n\n`:checkhealth` shows this warning\n\n```\nWARNING `focus-events` is not enabled. |'autoread'| may not work.\n  - ADVICE:\n    - (tmux 1.9+ only) Set `focus-events` in ~/.tmux.conf:\n      set-option -g focus-events on\n```\n\nI've done that and the warning refuses to go away.\n\n## Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Install tmux and neovim. I'm getting them from Homebrew on Bluefin Linux.\n2. Start `tmux`.\n3. Open `nvim` and run `:checkhealth`.\n\n## Expected behavior\n\nWarning goes away after I set the option\n\n## System info\n\n- Nvim version (nvim -v): `v0.12.4` neovim/neovim@\n- Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?: I have no idea - don't use regular vim any more\n- Operating system/version: Linux 7.1.4-ogc1\n- Terminal name/version: tmux 3.7b\n- $TERM environment variable: `tmux-256color`\n- Installation: From Homebrew on Bluefin Linux \n\n",
